# Sift Memory

Use `sift` as local memory search for prior AI coding-assistant sessions.

## Commands

Prefer the installed CLI:

```sh
sift index --json
sift "<query>" --limit 10 --json
sift "<query>" --tool codex --limit 10 --json
sift "<query>" --tool claude --limit 10 --json
sift "<query>" --tool cursor --limit 10 --json
sift "<query>" --tool opencode --limit 10 --json
sift show "<ref>" --json
sift list --limit 10 --json
```

When working inside the `sift` repo and the global command is unavailable, use:

```sh
node ./bin/sift.js index --json
node ./bin/sift.js "<query>" --limit 10 --json
node ./bin/sift.js show "<ref>" --json
node ./bin/sift.js list --limit 10 --json
```

Use `sift index --full` only when the user asks, parser/index behavior changed, or incremental results look stale.

## Behavior

- Search before answering when local session history could materially improve accuracy.
- Use focused queries based on project names, command names, file names, bug symptoms, package names, or prior decisions.
- Follow only relevant search refs with `sift show` when surrounding messages are needed.
- Summarize only relevant findings. Do not paste large raw logs.
- Keep the workflow local: no network calls, no telemetry, no sync, no writes to Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, or OpenCode source logs/databases.
